{"additionalPlain":"Why Join Assist World?\n \n100% REMOTE\n$50 birthday bonus\n$200 testimonial bonus\nNO TRACKER. NO PROBLEM\n","additional":"<div><strong>Why Join Assist World?</strong></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>100% REMOTE</div>\n<div>$50 birthday&nbsp;bonus</div>\n<div>$200 testimonial bonus</div>\n<div>NO TRACKER. NO PROBLEM</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Part-Time","location":"South Africa","team":"Virtual Assistant / Part-Time","allLocations":["South Africa","Philippines"]},"createdAt":1783380422415,"descriptionPlain":"About the Role\nWe are looking for a highly organized, detail-oriented Virtual Administrative & Agent Onboarding\nCoordinator to support our growing insurance agency. This role is focused on keeping\nprospective and newly recruited insurance agents engaged throughout the onboarding process,\nensuring they stay on track from initial interest through licensing and contracting.\n\nThis is an administrative and communication-focused position that requires excellent written\ncommunication, strong organizational skills, and the ability to manage multiple follow-ups\nsimultaneously.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n● Manage ongoing communication with prospective and newly recruited insurance agents\nprimarily via text messaging.\n● Monitor agents' progress through the onboarding pipeline, including:\n    ○ Exam scheduling\n    ○ Exam preparation\n    ○ Licensing\n    ○ Contracting\n● Conduct regular follow-ups (typically every 2–3 days) to keep agents engaged and\nmotivated throughout the process.\n● Respond to inquiries and provide the appropriate onboarding information based on each\nagent's current stage.\n● Route qualified prospects to the appropriate next step, including:\n    ○ Scheduling follow-up calls\n    ○ Sending exam registration information\n    ○ Initiating contracting paperwork for licensed agents\n● Maintain accurate notes and update all communication records within the company's\nCRM/database.\n● Assist with weekly lead follow-up after Thursday opportunity overview calls.\n● Help schedule appointments between interested candidates and leadership when\nneeded.\n● Take on additional administrative tasks as the business continues to grow.\n\nQualifications\n\n● Excellent written English communication skills.\n● Strong organizational and time-management abilities.\n● Comfortable managing multiple conversations simultaneously.\n● Detail-oriented with accurate record-keeping skills.\n● Proactive and consistent with follow-up.\n● Comfortable learning internal onboarding processes and workflows.\n● Ability to work independently while maintaining regular communication with leadership.\n● Previous administrative, virtual assistant, customer support, or client success experience is preferred but not required. \nPreferred Skills\n● Experience using CRMs or applicant tracking systems.\n● Experience with text-based customer communication.\n● Scheduling and calendar management experience.\n● Ability to quickly learn new software and internal processes.\n\nWhat We're Looking For\nThe ideal candidate is:\n● Highly dependable and responsive.\n● An excellent communicator.\n● Organized and process-driven.\n● Comfortable handling repetitive administrative tasks with accuracy.\n● Motivated to help people successfully complete their onboarding journey.\n\nSuccess in This Role\nSuccess will be measured by:\n● Consistent follow-up with all prospective and onboarding agents.\n● Increased engagement throughout the onboarding process.\n● Reduced administrative workload for leadership.\n● Timely movement of agents through the licensing and contracting pipeline.\nThis role is ideal for someone who enjoys organization, communication, and helping people stay\non track while working independently in a remote environment.\n","description":"<div><strong>About the Role</strong><br>We are looking for a highly organized, detail-oriented Virtual Administrative &amp; Agent Onboarding<br>Coordinator to support our growing insurance agency. This role is focused on keeping<br>prospective and newly recruited insurance agents engaged throughout the onboarding process,<br>ensuring they stay on track from initial interest through licensing and contracting.</div>\n<div><br>This is an administrative and communication-focused position that requires excellent written<br>communication, strong organizational skills, and the ability to manage multiple follow-ups<br>simultaneously.</div>\n<div><br><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong><br>● Manage ongoing communication with prospective and newly recruited insurance agents<br>primarily via text messaging.<br>● Monitor agents' progress through the onboarding pipeline, including:<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Exam scheduling<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Exam preparation<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Licensing<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Contracting<br>● Conduct regular follow-ups (typically every 2–3 days) to keep agents engaged and<br>motivated throughout the process.<br>● Respond to inquiries and provide the appropriate onboarding information based on each<br>agent's current stage.<br>● Route qualified prospects to the appropriate next step, including:<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Scheduling follow-up calls<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Sending exam registration information<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Initiating contracting paperwork for licensed agents<br>● Maintain accurate notes and update all communication records within the company's<br>CRM/database.<br>● Assist with weekly lead follow-up after Thursday opportunity overview calls.<br>● Help schedule appointments between interested candidates and leadership when<br>needed.<br>● Take on additional administrative tasks as the business continues to grow.<br><br><strong>Qualifications<br><br></strong></div>\n<div>● Excellent written English communication skills.<br>● Strong organizational and time-management abilities.<br>● Comfortable managing multiple conversations simultaneously.<br>● Detail-oriented with accurate record-keeping skills.<br>● Proactive and consistent with follow-up.<br>● Comfortable learning internal onboarding processes and workflows.<br>● Ability to work independently while maintaining regular communication with leadership.<br>● Previous administrative, virtual assistant, customer support, or client success experience is preferred but not required.\n<p><strong>Preferred Skills</strong><br>● Experience using CRMs or applicant tracking systems.<br>● Experience with text-based customer communication.<br>● Scheduling and calendar management experience.<br>● Ability to quickly learn new software and internal processes.</p>\n<p><br><strong>What We're Looking For</strong><br>The ideal candidate is:<br>● Highly dependable and responsive.<br>● An excellent communicator.<br>● Organized and process-driven.<br>● Comfortable handling repetitive administrative tasks with accuracy.<br>● Motivated to help people successfully complete their onboarding journey.</p>\n<p><br><strong>Success in This Role</strong><br>Success will be measured by:<br>● Consistent follow-up with all prospective and onboarding agents.<br>● Increased engagement throughout the onboarding process.<br>● Reduced administrative workload for leadership.<br>● Timely movement of agents through the licensing and contracting pipeline.</p>\n<p>This role is ideal for someone who enjoys organization, communication, and helping people stay<br>on track while working independently in a remote environment.</p>\n</div>","id":"11e92541-8799-4998-880f-c75772bea8b7","lists":[],"salaryRange":{"min":500,"max":800,"currency":"USD","interval":"per-month-salary"},"salaryDescription":"<div><strong>Weekly Workflow<br></strong>The workload is flexible, with approximately 20 hours per week.<br><br>Expected priorities include:<br>● <strong>Thursday evenings (Eastern Time):</strong> Follow up with new leads generated from the&nbsp;weekly opportunity call.<br>● <strong>Fridays:</strong> Continue lead follow-up and onboarding communications.<br>● <strong>Throughout the week:</strong> Check in with existing agents progressing through licensing and<br>onboarding to maintain engagement.</div>","salaryDescriptionPlain":"Weekly WorkflowThe workload is flexible, with approximately 20 hours per week.\n\nExpected priorities include:\n● Thursday evenings (Eastern Time): Follow up with new leads generated from the weekly opportunity call.\n● Fridays: Continue lead follow-up and onboarding communications.\n● Throughout the week: Check in with existing agents progressing through licensing and\nonboarding to maintain engagement.\n","text":"Virtual Administrative & Agent Onboarding Coordinator","country":"ZA","workplaceType":"remote","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div><strong>About the Role</strong><br>We are looking for a highly organized, detail-oriented Virtual Administrative &amp; Agent Onboarding<br>Coordinator to support our growing insurance agency. This role is focused on keeping<br>prospective and newly recruited insurance agents engaged throughout the onboarding process,<br>ensuring they stay on track from initial interest through licensing and contracting.</div>\n<div><br>This is an administrative and communication-focused position that requires excellent written<br>communication, strong organizational skills, and the ability to manage multiple follow-ups<br>simultaneously.</div>\n<div><br><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong><br>● Manage ongoing communication with prospective and newly recruited insurance agents<br>primarily via text messaging.<br>● Monitor agents' progress through the onboarding pipeline, including:<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Exam scheduling<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Exam preparation<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Licensing<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Contracting<br>● Conduct regular follow-ups (typically every 2&ndash;3 days) to keep agents engaged and<br>motivated throughout the process.<br>● Respond to inquiries and provide the appropriate onboarding information based on each<br>agent's current stage.<br>● Route qualified prospects to the appropriate next step, including:<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Scheduling follow-up calls<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Sending exam registration information<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ○ Initiating contracting paperwork for licensed agents<br>● Maintain accurate notes and update all communication records within the company's<br>CRM/database.<br>● Assist with weekly lead follow-up after Thursday opportunity overview calls.<br>● Help schedule appointments between interested candidates and leadership when<br>needed.<br>● Take on additional administrative tasks as the business continues to grow.<br><br><strong>Qualifications<br><br></strong></div>\n<div>● Excellent written English communication skills.<br>● Strong organizational and time-management abilities.<br>● Comfortable managing multiple conversations simultaneously.<br>● Detail-oriented with accurate record-keeping skills.<br>● Proactive and consistent with follow-up.<br>● Comfortable learning internal onboarding processes and workflows.<br>● Ability to work independently while maintaining regular communication with leadership.<br>● Previous administrative, virtual assistant, customer support, or client success experience is preferred but not required.\n<p><strong>Preferred Skills</strong><br>● Experience using CRMs or applicant tracking systems.<br>● Experience with text-based customer communication.<br>● Scheduling and calendar management experience.<br>● Ability to quickly learn new software and internal processes.</p>\n<p><br><strong>What We're Looking For</strong><br>The ideal candidate is:<br>● Highly dependable and responsive.<br>● An excellent communicator.<br>● Organized and process-driven.<br>● Comfortable handling repetitive administrative tasks with accuracy.<br>● Motivated to help people successfully complete their onboarding journey.</p>\n<p><br><strong>Success in This Role</strong><br>Success will be measured by:<br>● Consistent follow-up with all prospective and onboarding agents.<br>● Increased engagement throughout the onboarding process.<br>● Reduced administrative workload for leadership.<br>● Timely movement of agents through the licensing and contracting pipeline.</p>\n<p>This role is ideal for someone who enjoys organization, communication, and helping people stay<br>on track while working independently in a remote environment.</p>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"About the Role\nWe are looking for a highly organized, detail-oriented Virtual Administrative & Agent Onboarding\nCoordinator to support our growing insurance agency. This role is focused on keeping\nprospective and newly recruited insurance agents engaged throughout the onboarding process,\nensuring they stay on track from initial interest through licensing and contracting.\n\nThis is an administrative and communication-focused position that requires excellent written\ncommunication, strong organizational skills, and the ability to manage multiple follow-ups\nsimultaneously.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n● Manage ongoing communication with prospective and newly recruited insurance agents\nprimarily via text messaging.\n● Monitor agents' progress through the onboarding pipeline, including:\n    ○ Exam scheduling\n    ○ Exam preparation\n    ○ Licensing\n    ○ Contracting\n● Conduct regular follow-ups (typically every 2–3 days) to keep agents engaged and\nmotivated throughout the process.\n● Respond to inquiries and provide the appropriate onboarding information based on each\nagent's current stage.\n● Route qualified prospects to the appropriate next step, including:\n    ○ Scheduling follow-up calls\n    ○ Sending exam registration information\n    ○ Initiating contracting paperwork for licensed agents\n● Maintain accurate notes and update all communication records within the company's\nCRM/database.\n● Assist with weekly lead follow-up after Thursday opportunity overview calls.\n● Help schedule appointments between interested candidates and leadership when\nneeded.\n● Take on additional administrative tasks as the business continues to grow.\n\nQualifications\n\n● Excellent written English communication skills.\n● Strong organizational and time-management abilities.\n● Comfortable managing multiple conversations simultaneously.\n● Detail-oriented with accurate record-keeping skills.\n● Proactive and consistent with follow-up.\n● Comfortable learning internal onboarding processes and workflows.\n● Ability to work independently while maintaining regular communication with leadership.\n● Previous administrative, virtual assistant, customer support, or client success experience is preferred but not required. \nPreferred Skills\n● Experience using CRMs or applicant tracking systems.\n● Experience with text-based customer communication.\n● Scheduling and calendar management experience.\n● Ability to quickly learn new software and internal processes.\n\nWhat We're Looking For\nThe ideal candidate is:\n● Highly dependable and responsive.\n● An excellent communicator.\n● Organized and process-driven.\n● Comfortable handling repetitive administrative tasks with accuracy.\n● Motivated to help people successfully complete their onboarding journey.\n\nSuccess in This Role\nSuccess will be measured by:\n● Consistent follow-up with all prospective and onboarding agents.\n● Increased engagement throughout the onboarding process.\n● Reduced administrative workload for leadership.\n● Timely movement of agents through the licensing and contracting pipeline.\nThis role is ideal for someone who enjoys organization, communication, and helping people stay\non track while working independently in a remote environment.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/assist-world/11e92541-8799-4998-880f-c75772bea8b7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/assist-world/11e92541-8799-4998-880f-c75772bea8b7/apply"}